## What Problem This Solves

Fixes repeated secret-provider executions when an auth-store revision invalidates a secrets snapshot refresh.

Fixes #173611

## Why This Change Was Made

Refresh retries now share one per-refresh SecretRef cache. Batch resolution reuses successful refs and sends only uncached refs to the provider.

## User Impact

An unchanged external secret reference is resolved once even when the refresh must retry after an auth-store revision changes.

## Evidence

- Focused regression tests: `OPENCLAW_VITEST_RUNTIME=node node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/secrets/runtime.test.ts src/secrets/resolve.mixed-failures.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 -t "repeated auth-store revision invalidations|reuses cached refs while batching newly requested provider refs" --reporter=dot` — 2 passed, 18 skipped. The integration case exercises an actual exec-provider subprocess; the resolver case confirms cached batch refs are reused while newly requested refs remain batched.
- Real production path on base `4691afa4f88f8aa41c0d275e9a1988c81649d055`: the same `node_modules/.bin/tsx proof-live.mts .` command succeeded after three auth-store revision invalidations but called the exec provider three times.
- Same command and input on head `482533bf908883805ce614050120d4c755d7eeaf`: refresh succeeded after the same three invalidations and called the exec provider once.
- Negative control: the production snapshot path still rejects an invalid exec SecretRef id.
- The implementation extends the existing `SecretRefResolveCache` contract in `src/secrets/resolve-types.ts`.

