Related implementation: #140067. That existing PR addresses the same reported timeout; this draft offers a narrower connection/response deadline separation for comparison.

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: macOS companion commands report `COMPANION_APP_UNAVAILABLE` after 20 seconds when the command is still running within its requested timeout.

## User Impact

User impact: commands that take longer than 20 seconds can return their completion or native process-timeout receipt. Deployment to the bundled Mac node worker still requires a new signed macOS app release; this patch has not been installed into an existing signed app.

## Why This Change Was Made

Keep the default 20-second connection deadline, then use the requested process timeout plus 10 seconds of response grace once connected. A nonpositive or absent process timeout leaves response lifetime to cancellation or peer closure. An explicitly supplied transport timeout retains its existing behavior. Request signing, approval handling, and response cleanup remain intact.

This draft was prepared with Codex assistance.

## Evidence

- Installed macOS app 2026.9.7 reproduction: `/usr/bin/true` succeeds; `/bin/sleep 22` with a 35-second process budget fails at approximately 20 seconds with the companion-unavailable error.
- Supplemental fake-timer test over real Unix-domain sockets: baseline fails three lifetime cases; the candidate passes all four, including late completion, native timeout receipt, explicit transport deadline, and cancellation.
- Repository validation: `pnpm test src/infra/exec-host.test.ts src/infra/exec-host.socket.test.ts src/infra/jsonl-socket.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` passes all 23 tests across three files (4.66 seconds command wall time). New socket regression cases use fake timers with real sockets and add no wall-clock sleep.
- `pnpm check:changed`, formatting, and `git diff --check` pass. Production types and all 10 relevant test type-check groups pass.
- Required autoreview completed with no accepted actionable findings in the changed scope.
- Local validation used base `6aa12006ff81ee0ba2c72eaafc41ea196c8600e7`; the published branch starts from `5c894c71b889408c0bf583ae4aa08e36129ab3a4`. The intervening commit changes only unrelated gateway worker bootstrap files. All four published file blobs match the tested files.

Remaining validation: upstream CI and an end-to-end run of a newly built, signed macOS app. The full repository test suite and full app build were not run locally.

